ars old and<br/>then over 2 years old and</p><p begin="00:05:49.3" end="00:05:52.2">specific about adding sugar and<br/>things like that.</p><p begin="00:05:54.7" end="00:06:01.9">The 2nd guideline, you really want to<br/>customize that, that nutritional plan.</p><p begin="00:06:01.9" end="00:06:06.3">So that you have a nice mix of<br/>the nutrient dense foods and</p><p begin="00:06:06.3" end="00:06:11.2">beverages where you are going to take the<br/>consideration on cultural competency as</p><p begin="00:06:11.2" end="00:06:14.8">well as budgetary considerations for<br/>each patient.</p><p begin="00:06:14.8" end="00:06:19.6">So it's not a one size fits all for every<br/>patient when it comes to what a healthy,</p><p begin="00:06:19.6" end="00:06:22.6">dietary or<br/>nutritional plan looks like for them.</p><p begin="00:06:24.2" end="00:06:28.2">The 3rd guidelines focuses on<br/>meeting your food group need.</p><p begin="00:06:28.2" end="00:06:31.3">making sure most of that is what<br/>they are nutrients then food and</p><p begin="00:06:31.3" end="00:06:35.7">beverages while staying<br/>within your calorie limits.</p><p begin="00:06:35.7" end="00:06:36.9">Ok.</p><p begin="00:06:36.9" end="00:06:42.3">So here it's really not about<br/>the quantity of your calories,</p><p begin="00:06:42.3" end="00:06:44.9">like if you've ever used any<br/>of those calorie calculators.</p><p begin="00:06:44.9" end="00:06:48.6">You know, like I could get like,<br/>you know, 2000 calorie of a day.</p><p begin="00:06:48.6" end="00:06:52.9">It's the quality of those<br/>calories that are most important.</p><p begin="00:06:52.9" end="00:06:56.1">And we'll discuss that<br/>further in today's lecture.</p><p begin="00:06:57.3" end="00:06:58.9">And then the 4th guideline is limiting.</p><p begin="00:06:58.9" end="00:07:03">If we can, beverages that are higher and<br/>things such as added sugars,</p><p begin="00:07:03" end="00:07:07.8">saturated fat and sodium,<br/>while also limiting alcoholic beverage,</p><p begin="00:07:07.8" end="00:07:12.6">is lizzy a for mean guidelines.</p><p begin="00:07:12.6" end="00:07:15.7">That 1st guideline really does focus on</p><p begin="00:07:16.8" end="00:07:21.5">how healthy dietary pattern and<br/>each life stage is important.</p><p begin="00:07:21.5" end="00:07:24.5">So some of the main things,</p><p begin="00:07:24.5" end="00:07:29.7">this is one of the main<br/>changes from the 2015 to 2020</p><p begin="00:07:29.7" end="00:07:34.4">dietary guidelines where they're<br/>really talking about each life stage.</p><p begin="00:07:35.7" end="00:07:38.10">So primarily when we're talking about</p><p begin="00:07:38.10" end="00:07:43.2">from the 1st 6 months alive to<br/>about a year of why, you know,</p><p begin="00:07:43.2" end="00:07:47.2">you really want to aim for reading<br/>infants with human or breastfeeding.</p><p begin="00:07:48.10" end="00:07:54.6">There's more information on that on<br/>slide 18 and 19 of my presentation.</p><p begin="00:07:56.3" end="00:08:00.1">Also talking about when<br/>you supplement vitamin b,</p><p begin="00:08:00.1" end="00:08:05.5">when do you start to introduce<br/>food into an infant diet</p><p begin="00:08:05.5" end="00:08:10.3">that usually start around 6 months, but<br/>again, you want to focus on nutrient and</p><p begin="00:08:10.3" end="00:08:14.10">then that is going to compliment what the<br/>breath nope can provide for the patient.</p><p begin="00:08:18.7" end="00:08:21.7">And that is from 12 months<br/>through older adulthood,</p><p begin="00:08:21.7" end="00:08:24.8">we're going to talk a little<br/>bit more about that as well.</p><p begin="00:08:24.8" end="00:08:29.2">So it's making sure you have<br/>a well balanced nutrient</p><p begin="00:08:30.2" end="00:08:34.4">rich plan throughout your life.</p><p begin="00:08:34.4" end="00:08:37.3">This will reduce the risk<br/>of chronic disease</p><p begin="00:08:41.10" end="00:08:46.9">You want to customize, enjoy your<br/>new trad